<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 1 August, from 30 BCE to 1944.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexandria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,055 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Octavian takes Alexandria and Mark Antony takes his own life</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Octavian's army entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, defeated and deserted, killed himself. Cleopatra's suicide days later ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic dynasty</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> became a Roman province.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">902 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,124 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ibrahim II of Ifriqiya captures Taormina from the Byzantines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aghlabid forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-ii-of-ifriqiya">Ibrahim II of Ifriqiya</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taormina">Taormina</a>, the last great citadel in Byzantine hands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, after volunteers climbed its unwatched seaward face. Its fall concluded the Muslim conquest of Sicily.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taormina">Taormina</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-ii-of-ifriqiya">Ibrahim II of Ifriqiya</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabid dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1291">1291 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">735 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swiss cantons swear the alliance celebrated as Switzerland's birth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Uri, Schwyz and Unterwalden concluded a perpetual defensive alliance, recorded in the Federal Charter dated early August 1291. 1 August is now Swiss National Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1714">1714 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">312 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Anne dies, ending the Stuart line</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Queen Anne died without surviving children, the last Stuart monarch. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701">Act of Settlement</a> the crown passed to George, Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, beginning the Hanoverian dynasty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1774">1774 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">252 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph Priestley isolates oxygen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By heating mercuric oxide, Joseph Priestley produced a gas in which a candle burned with remarkable vigour. He called it 'dephlogisticated air'; Lavoisier later named it oxygen.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France's Convention adopts the metric system</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> decreed a provisional metre, based on a fraction of the Earth's meridian, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s unit of length. The decimal metric system has since been adopted almost worldwide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany declares war on Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> refused to halt mobilisation, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> declared war on it. The declaration turned the Austro-Serbian conflict into a general European war within days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Warsaw Uprising begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Polish Home Army rose against the German occupiers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>. After 63 days, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> halted across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>, the uprising was crushed and the city systematically destroyed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 1 August <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hyeonjong-of-goryeo"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Hyeonjong of Goryeo</span><span class="tp">992–1031</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-jin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-taizu-of-jin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Taizu of Jin</span><span class="tp">1068–1123</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-komatsu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-go-komatsu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Go-Komatsu</span><span class="tp">1377–1433</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-prince-of-anhalt-kothen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wolfgang-prince-of-anhalt-kothen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wolfgang, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen</span><span class="tp">1492–1566</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/konstantinos-logothetopoulos"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Konstantinos Logothetopoulos</span><span class="tp">1878–1961</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexander-of-greece"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexander-of-greece.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander of Greece</span><span class="tp">1893–1920</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hafizullah-amin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hafizullah-amin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hafizullah Amin</span><span class="tp">1929–1979</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kurmanbek-bakiyev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kurmanbek-bakiyev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kurmanbek Bakiyev</span><span class="tp">b. 1949</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 1 August <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adhemar-of-le-puy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adhemar-of-le-puy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adhemar of Le Puy</span><span class="tp">d. 1098</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-vi-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-vi-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis VI of France</span><span class="tp">1081–1137</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-valla"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lorenzo-valla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lorenzo Valla</span><span class="tp">c. 1407–1457</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cosimo-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cosimo de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1389–1464</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jind-kaur"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jind-kaur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jind Kaur</span><span class="tp">1817–1863</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-ross-cherokee-chief"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-ross-cherokee-chief.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Ross (Cherokee chief)</span><span class="tp">1790–1866</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-l-quezon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-l-quezon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel L. Quezon</span><span class="tp">1878–1944</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/corazon-aquino"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/corazon-aquino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Corazon Aquino</span><span class="tp">1933–2009</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
